  "preconditions": [
    "0x00403640: a3 is a non-null spatial-tree root whose children are linked at +0x10C (prev) and +0x110 (next); this[76]>0 requires a valid stride-316 array at this[77].",
    "0x00406130: CreateMutexA may fail; slot flags tolerate a null handle.",
    "0x00406790: this+8 must point to a valid Miles mixer/driver object whose +0x90 offset is a usable AIL driver handle; this+16 is an optional literal stream name.",
    "0x00407520: a2 must be non-null; the file resource referenced by the aRb path must be present for the insert to succeed.",
    "0x00411840: a1 must point to a font/character descriptor; the font globals (byte_5EA5E0 guard) are lazily initialized on first call.",
    "0x00411B50: a1 is a character code; when a2 is 0 or 1 it indexes the unk_5BEE08/unk_5BF4C0 tables, which must be initialized.",
    "0x00414900: a1 is a non-null path string; FileName stack buffer is 256 bytes and the input is truncated to 250 chars.",
    "0x00414370: reads *this; caller must not pass a pointer that makes the deref invalid."
  ],
  "postconditions": [
    "0x00403640: returns pointer to the nearest spatial node (or 0 when a3 was null); the 30.0-unit radius filter decides between the tree best and the array best.",
    "0x00404E60: returns the new node pointer (0 on allocation failure); string list head/tail/count at +0x40/+0x44/+0x4C are updated.",
    "0x00404EF0: returns the result of the wrapped string-copy helper.",
    "0x00405440/0x004057F0/0x004149A0: the target struct is left fully initialized with sentinel -1 / empty-string defaults; 0x004057F0 also stores a vtable pointer (off_59E490) and returns this.",
    "0x00406130: six 20-byte audio slots are initialized, a Win32 mutex handle is stored at +0x50 with the +0x58 flag set on success, vtable finalized to off_59E4EC; returns this.",
    "0x00406790: on success this+12 holds the opened AIL stream handle and it is registered/started/volume-set; on failure the three audio slots are cleared.",
    "0x004069F0: this+0x5C holds the loaded stream file handle (or -1) and this[7] participates in the generated mp3 name; returns this[0x5C] != -1.",
    "0x00407450/0x00407520: a new node is appended at the sorted position; list count at +0x34/+0x44 increments; 0x00407520 returns 1 on success, 0 otherwise.",
    "0x00408870/0x0040AA20: sound-emitter slots (this[9..12], this[4..8]) hold allocated F_3DSoundEmitter objects with 384.0/512.0-style position constants written at +0x88/+0x8C/+0x90.",
    "0x00411840: returns the count (0-3) of character events dispatched; font-prep globals are (re)initialized.",
    "0x00411B50: on success writes {a1, mapped-code} into a3+8/+0xC and returns 0; returns 1 on unmapped code.",
    "0x00411DB0: on success writes code/selector/flag into a4+8/+0xC/+0x10 and returns 1; returns -1 for the special 9875/9876 unhandled cases.",
    "0x004122C0/0x004133B0/0x004134D0/0x00413600/0x00413710: fill a1 text slot from the selected lookup entry; return -1 when the slot is empty, 1 otherwise.",
    "0x00414900: on success fills a2+8/+0xC with -1 and +0x10 with 0 and returns 0; returns 1 when the win32 attribute check fails.",
    "0x00414370: frees *this via FreeWrapper_7bcf and returns the old value (or 0 if it was null)."
  ],
  "side_effects": [
    "0x00404E60/0x00407450/0x00407520: heap allocations via OperatorNewNhMallocWrapper (8+12-byte string/list nodes; 116-byte file entry node) and appends to embedded linked lists.",
    "0x00406130: creates a Win32 mutex (CreateMutexA) and holds its handle in object state.",
    "0x00406790: opens and starts a Miles audio stream (AIL_open_stream/AIL_start_stream), registers a callback, sets volume; writes the handle into this+12.",
    "0x004069F0: loads a stream file handle into this+0x5C and mutates the internal stream-name state (this[23]).",
    "0x00411840: init-once writes of dword_5EA5D0..DC and the byte_5EA5E0 guard flag; dispatches character events which may decrement caller counters.",
    "0x004122C0/0x004133B0/0x004134D0/0x00413600/0x00413710: copy the selected entry's string into the out slot (a1) and its +8/+0xC/+0x10 fields.",
    "0x00414900: copies the checked filename into a1 and writes sentinels into a2; queries a win32 file-attribute API.",
    "0x00414370: releases heap memory through FreeWrapper_7bcf.",
    "0x00405440/0x004057F0/0x00406130/0x00408870: vtable-pointer writes and scalar field initializations on the target objects."
  ],
